\section{Acquisition protocol}{


The data were acquired using the following setup. More information
can be found in the source article (see \code{References}).
\itemize{
\item \strong{Cell isolation}: CellenONE cell sorting.
\item \strong{Sample preparation}: performed using the improved SCoPE2
protocol using the CellenONE liquid handling system: nPOP cell lysis
(DMSO) + trypsin digestion + mTRAQ 3-plex labelling.
\item \strong{Separation}: online nLC (NanoElute2) with a 25cm x 75um IonOpticks
Aurora column and captive spray fitting (LC gradient 4-38\% buffer B).
\item \strong{Mass spectrometry}: timsTOF Ultra mass spectrometer.
\item \strong{Data analysis}: DIA-NN.
}
}

\section{Data collection}{


The PSM data were collected from a massIVE repository (see \code{Source} section).
The folder \code{f.MSV000093494/search} contains the following
file of interest:
\itemize{
\item \code{report.tsv}: PSM-level quantitative data
}

Sample metadata were collected from a shared Google Drive folder that
is accessible from the SlavovLab website (see \code{Source} section).
The folder contains the following files of interest:
\itemize{
\item \code{plexDIA_SingleCell_Meta.csv}: sample-level annotations
\item \code{plexDIA_SingleCellxProtein.csv}: processed protein-level data table
provided by the authors, containing the \code{imported_proteins} data
}

We formatted sample-level annotations to ensure columns match with those
of the quantification tables. Sample annotations containing \code{NA} values for
\code{neg} samples were manually filled in based on the \code{ID} column in order
to circumvent duplicate sample naming errors. These changes are incorporated
in the file \code{plexDIA_SingleCellxProtein_modified.csv}, available on
\href{https://doi.org/0.5281/zenodo.24020222}{Zenodo}.

Both quantification and annotation tables were then
combined in a single \link[QFeatures:QFeatures]{QFeatures} object using \code{\link[QFeatures:readQFeatures]{QFeatures::readQFeatures()}}.

The script to reproduce the QFeatures object is available at inst/scripts/make-data_leduc2024_plexDIA.R.
